  "version": "opposition_decks_v1",
  "description": "Phase 5b.5 \u00e2\u20ac\u201d curated registry of standardized opposition decks for MPA calibration. Each entry pins a corpus deck as a 'known opponent' at a given bracket. role_tag is the stable identifier the calibration suite uses to pick matchups; role_tags are unique within a bracket.",
  "selection_rationale": {
    "B1": "Exhibition tier \u00e2\u20ac\u201d pick archetype-diverse low-power decks. Pillow-fort, tokens, midrange.",
    "B2": "Core tier \u00e2\u20ac\u201d anchor on the 7 Wizards-published precons present in corpus_v1.json. These are the canonical 'known-weak' opposition; calibration uses them as the B2 floor.",
    "B3": "Upgraded tier \u00e2\u20ac\u201d pick across tribal / aristocrats-combo / pillow-fort-control to span the B3 spread.",
    "B4": "Optimized tier \u00e2\u20ac\u201d prefer entries whose archetype hint contains 'combo', 'stax', or 'cEDH-adjacent'. These are most likely to produce decisive games at MAX_TURNS=50.",
    "B5": "cEDH tier \u00e2\u20ac\u201d picks across combo / tempo / control-stax archetypes."
  },
